<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seraikela Kharsawan district</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seraikela Kharsawan is a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jharkhand">Jharkhand</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, created in 2001 from West Singhbhum district, with its headquarters at Seraikela. It is named after the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of Seraikela and Kharsawan, which merged with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Orissa</a> in 1948 and were transferred to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a> later that year. The area is known for the Seraikela style of the masked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhau-dance">Chhau dance</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seraikela-kharsawan-district.jpg" alt="Seraikela Kharsawan district" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anupmahato · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chandil_Dam.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
